# NexRouter line-ending and attribute rules
# ==========================================
# This project ships files that execute on an OpenWrt router, where /bin/sh is
# busybox ash. A CRLF line ending is not cosmetic there — it is fatal:
#
#   * A shell script whose shebang line ends "\r\n" is executed as
#     "/bin/sh\r", which does not exist, so the script fails to run at all.
#   * `uci-defaults` and `init.d` scripts with CRLF can mis-parse or silently
#     no-op.
#   * The tab-separated OUI table (oui.txt) parsed by awk/jq would carry a
#     trailing \r on every vendor name.
#
# Git's core.autocrlf can convert LF to CRLF on checkout (the default on many
# Windows setups, as the build here warned). These rules pin the files that MUST
# stay LF regardless of the cloner's platform, so `build/build.sh` works for
# anyone who clones on Windows/WSL/Linux. Text that is only ever read by humans
# or by Node is left to auto.

# Default: let Git normalise text files to LF in the repo, and do not surprise
# anyone on checkout.
* text=auto eol=lf

# ── Must be LF: executed on the router or by a POSIX shell ───────────────────
*.sh          text eol=lf
build/files/** text eol=lf
# The firmware overlay files have no extension but are shell/UCI/JSON:
99-nexrouter-firstboot text eol=lf
nexrouter              text eol=lf
nexrouter-core         text eol=lf
nexrouter-insight      text eol=lf
insight-query          text eol=lf
config/nexrouter       text eol=lf

# ── Must be LF: machine-parsed data ──────────────────────────────────────────
# oui.txt is TAB-separated and read field-by-field; a trailing \r corrupts it.
*.tsv         text eol=lf
oui.txt       text eol=lf
*.csv         text eol=lf
*.json        text eol=lf

# ── Source read by Node / the browser (LF keeps diffs clean) ─────────────────
*.js          text eol=lf
*.mjs         text eol=lf
*.css         text eol=lf
*.html        text eol=lf
*.md          text eol=lf

# ── Firmware images and other true binaries: never touch ─────────────────────
*.bin         binary
*.img         binary
*.png         binary
*.jpg         binary
*.ico         binary
*.gz          binary
*.xz          binary
